0	section	Talking to Brundt the Chieftain
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What is this place?
2	line	Player	What is this place?
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	This place? Why, this is Rellekka! Homeland of all Fremennik! I do not recognise your face outerlander; Where do you come from?
2	line	Player	That's not important...
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Hmmm... I will not press the issue then outerlander. How may my tribe and I help you?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Do you have any quests?
3	line	Player	Do you have any quests?
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Quests, you say outerlander? Well, I would not call it a quest as such, but if you are brave of heart and strong of body, perhaps...
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	No, you would not be interested. Forget I said anything, outerlander.
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Yes, I am interested.
4	line	Player	Actually, I would be very interested to hear what you have to offer.
4	line	Brundt the Chieftain	You would? These are unusual sentiments to hear from an outerlander! My suggestion was going to be that if you crave adventure and battle,
4	line	Brundt the Chieftain	and your heart sings for glory, then perhaps you would be interested in joining our clan, and becoming a Fremennik yourself?
4	line	Player	What would that involve exactly?
4	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Well, there are two ways to become a member of our clan and call yourself a Fremennik: be born a Fremennik, or be voted in by our council of elders.
4	line	Player	Well, I think I've missed the first way, but how can I get the council of elders to vote to let me join your clan?
4	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Well, that I cannot answer myself. You will need to speak to each of them and see what they require of you as proof of your dedication.
4	line	Brundt the Chieftain	There are twelve council members around this village; you will need to gain a majority vote of at least seven councillors in your favour.
4	line	Brundt the Chieftain	So what say you? Give me the word, and I will tell all of my tribe of your intentions, be they yea or nay.
4	cond	If the player is missing at least one requirement before starting the quest:
5	box	Before starting this quest, be aware that one or more of your skill levels are lower than what is required to fully complete it.
5	action	continues
4	select	Start The Fremennik Trials quest?
5	option	Yes.
6	line	Player	I think I would enjoy the challenge of becoming an honorary Fremennik. Where and how do I start?
6	line	Brundt the Chieftain	As I say outerlander, you must find and speak to the twelve members of the council of elders, and see what tasks they might set you.
6	line	Brundt the Chieftain	If you can gain the support of seven of the twelve, then you will be accepted as one of us without question.
6	action	end
5	option	No.
6	line	Player	No way do I want to become like YOU! Forget you, and forget your whole stupid town! You're a bunch of stupid primitives, from what I've seen!
6	line	Brundt the Chieftain	I am sorry to say that I expected such a response from an outerlander. I thought perhaps you might have been different to all the others...
6	action	end
3	option	No, I'm not interested.
4	line	Player	You're right. I really couldn't care less.
4	line	Brundt the Chieftain	It is as I thought outerlander. Your kind care nothing for the Fremennik, and we feel the same about you. This is the way of the world.
4	action	end
2	option	Why will no-one talk to me?
3	line	Player	Why will no-one talk to me?
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Do not take it personally, outerlander! We are a simple people, and it is our experience that keeping ourselves to ourselves is best. This is why speaking to outerlanders is forbidden.
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	We do not wish to enter war with the outerlanders and their strange magics, so we limit all unauthorised communication.
3	line	Player	Then how come you're talking to me?
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Ah, this is because I am the chieftain. I am the one who authorises contact. You will not find many of my tribe so forthcoming with you, as I.
3	line	Player	Is there a way for you to authorise your tribe to talk to me then?
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Well, there is one way... but I doubt it is of any interest to you.
3	line	Player	Actually, I would be very interested to hear what you have to offer.
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	You would? These are unusual sentiments to hear from an outerlander! My suggestion was going to be that if you crave adventure and battle,
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	and your heart sings for glory, then perhaps you would be interested in joining our clan, and becoming a Fremennik yourself?
3	line	Player	What would that involve exactly?
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Well, there are two ways to become a member of our clan and call yourself a Fremennik: be born a Fremennik, or be voted in by our council of elders.
3	line	Player	Well, I think I've missed the first way, but how can I get the council of elders to vote to let me join your clan?
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Well, that I cannot answer myself. You will need to speak to each of them and see what they require of you as proof of your dedication.
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	There are twelve council members around this village; you will need to gain a majority vote of at least seven councillors in your favour.
3	line	Brundt the Chieftain	So what say you? Give me the word, and I will tell all of my tribe of your intentions, be they yea or nay.
