0	section	The Council Members
0	section	Manni the Reveller
1	line	Player	Hello there!
1	line	Manni the Reveller	Hello outerlander. I overheard your conversation with Brundt just now. You wish to become a member of the Fremennik?
1	line	Player	That's right! Why, are you on the council?
1	line	Manni the Reveller	Do not let my drink-soused appearance fool you, I earnt my place on the council many years past. I am always glad to see new blood enter our tribe, and will happily vote for you.
1	line	Player	Great!
1	line	Manni the Reveller	...Providing you can pass a little test for me. As a Fremennik, you will need to show cunning, stamina, fortitude, and an iron constitution. I know of only one way to test all of these.
1	line	Player	And what's that?
1	line	Manni the Reveller	Why, a drinking contest!
1	line	Manni the Reveller	The task is simple enough! You versus me, a stiff drink each, last man standing wins the trial. So what say you?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Yes
2	line	Player	A drinking contest? Easy. Set them up, and I'll knock them back.
2	cond	If the player does not already have the tankard and/or beer tankard:
3	line	Manni the Reveller	When you are ready to begin, go and pick up a keg from that table over there, and come back here.
3	line	Manni the Reveller	We start when you have your keg of beer with you, and finish when one of us can drink no more and yields.
2	action	end
1	option	No
2	line	Player	I don't think drinking myself into a stupor is a very good way of testing my worthiness.
2	line	Manni the Reveller	Well, perhaps it's not, but it's my way. If you want my vote at the council, I'm afraid you're going to have to drink me under the table.
2	line	Player	I'm going to find someone else to vote for me then.
2	line	Manni the Reveller	As you wish, outerlander.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Manni the Reveller again
