0	section	Talking to the Council workman
1	line	Player	Hello.
1	line	Council workman	How do. You planning on crossing this here bridge and heading up to Rellekka then?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Yes
2	line	Player	Yes, actually I was.
2	line	Council workman	Aye, 'tis a good thing we fixed this 'ere bridge, I reckon. You best be careful up there. Them Fremenniks are odd 'uns.
2	line	Player	So you fixed this bridge yourself?
2	line	Council workman	Aye, that I did. 'Twas real thirsty work too. If only some kind stranger would buy us a bit of beer to sup, eh?
2	line	Council workman	What with that inn at seers so close by and all, eh?
2	box	The workman winks at you.
2	line	Council workman	Just make sure yer don't get me none of that non alcoholic rubbish from that poison salesman guy at the tavern!
2	action	end
1	option	No
2	line	Council workman	Aye, that's what I told t'gaffer. Nobody wants to go up and hang out with a buncha dumb barbarians when there's a perfectly good inn to sup in, in t'seers village.
2	line	Council workman	Ain't much better in life than having a nice cold beer to sup on a hot day like this, eh? Better'n fixing bridges, eh?
2	box	The workman winks at you.
2	line	Council workman	Just make sure yer don't get me none of that non alcoholic rubbish from that poison salesman guy at the tavern!
2	action	end
0	section	Using a normal beer or beer tankard on the Council workman
1	line	Council workman	Ta very much, like. That'll hit the spot nicely. Here, you can have this. I picked it up as a souvenir on me last hols.
1	action	
1	line	Player	What is it?
1	line	Council workman	I dunno rightly, but if you use a tinderbox on it, it don't half make a loud noise!
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to the Poison Salesman
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Talk about the Murder Mystery Quest
1	option	Talk about the Fremennik Trials
2	line	Player	Hello.
2	line	Poison Salesman	Howdy! You seem like someone with discerning taste! Howsabout you try my brand new range of alcohol?
2	line	Player	Didn't you used to sell poison?
2	line	Poison Salesman	That I did, indeed! Peter Potter's Patented Multipurpose poison! A miracle of modern apothecarys! My exclusive concoction has been tested on...
2	line	Player	Uh, yeah, I've already heard the sales pitch.
2	line	Poison Salesman	Sorry stranger, old habits die hard I guess.
2	line	Player	So you don't sell poison any more?
2	line	Poison Salesman	Well, I would, but I ran out of stock. Business wasn't helped with that stuff that happened up at the Sinclair Mansion much either, I'll be honest.
2	line	Poison Salesman	So, being the man of enterprise that I am I decided to branch out a little bit!
2	line	Player	Into alcohol?
2	line	Poison Salesman	Absolutely! The basic premise between alcohol and poison is pretty much the same, after all! The difference is that my alcohol has a unique property others do not!
2	line	Player	And what is that?
2	box	The salesman takes a deep breath.
2	line	Poison Salesman	Ever been too drunk to find your own home? Ever wished that you could party away all night long, and still wake up fresh as a daisy the next morning?
2	line	Poison Salesman	Thanks to the miracles of modern magic we have come up with just the solution you need! Peter Potter's Patented Party Potions!
2	line	Poison Salesman	It looks just like beer! It tastes just like beer! It smells just like beer! But... it's not beer!
2	line	Poison Salesman	Our mages have mused for many moments to bring you this miracle of modern magic! It has all the great tastes you'd expect, but contains absolutely no alcohol!
2	line	Poison Salesman	That's right! You can drink Peter Potters Patented Party Potion as much as you want, and suffer absolutely no ill effects whatsoever!
2	line	Poison Salesman	The clean fresh taste you know you can trust, from the people who brought you; Peter Potters Patented multipurpose poison, Peter Potters peculiar paint packs
2	line	Poison Salesman	and Peter Potters paralysing panic pins. Available now from all good stockists! Ask your local bartender now, and experience the taste revolution of the century!
2	box	He seems to have finished for the time being.
2	line	Player	So... when you say 'all good stockists'...
2	line	Poison Salesman	Yes?
2	line	Player	How many inns actually sell this stuff?
2	line	Poison Salesman	Well... nobody has actually bought any yet. Everyone I try and sell it to always asks me what exactly the point of beer that has absolutely no effect on you is.
2	line	Player	So what is the point?
2	line	Poison Salesman	Well... Um... Er... Hmmm. You, er, don't get drunk.
2	line	Player	I see...
2	line	Poison Salesman	Aw man... You don't want any now do you? I've really tried to push this product, but I just don't think the world is ready for beer that doesn't get you drunk.
2	line	Poison Salesman	I'm a man ahead of my time I tell you! It's not that my products are bad, it's that they're too good for the market!
2	line	Player	Actually, I would like some. How much do you want for it?
2	line	Poison Salesman	Y-you would??? Um, okay! I knew I still had the old salesmans skills going on!
2	line	Poison Salesman	I'll sell you a keg of it for only 250 gold pieces! So what do you say?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Yes
3	line	Player	Yes please!
3	cond	If the player does not have 250 gp:
4	line	Poison Salesman	Sorry pal, we do not offer credit for any purchases made of Peter Potter's patented party potion! Come back when you have the cash!
3	cond	If the player has 250 gp:
4	cond	If the player does not have inventory space:
5	line	Poison Salesman	Sorry pal, doesn't look like you have room on you to carry it.
5	action	end
4	cond	If the player has inventory space:
5	action	
5	action	end
2	option	No
3	line	Player	No, not really.
3	action	end
