0	section	Talking to him again
1	line	Player	So how would I go about writing this epic?
1	line	Olaf the Bard	Well, first of all you are going to need an instrument. Like all true bards you are going to have to make this yourself.
1	line	Player	How do I make an instrument?
1	line	Olaf the Bard	Well, it is a long and drawn-out process. Just east of this village there is an unusually musical tree that can be used to make very high quality instruments.
1	line	Olaf the Bard	Cut a piece from it, and then carve it into a special shape that will allow you to string it. Using a knife as you would craft any other wooden object would be best for this.
1	line	Player	Then what do I need to do?
1	line	Olaf the Bard	Next you will need to string your lyre. There is a troll to the South-east who has some golden wool. I would not recommend using anything else to string your lyre with.
1	line	Player	Anything else?
1	line	Olaf the Bard	Well, when you have crafted your lyre you will need the blessing of the Fossegrimen to tune your lyre to perfection before you even consider a public performance.
1	line	Player	Who or what is Fossegrimen?
1	line	Olaf the Bard	Fossegrimen is a lake spirit that lives just a little way South-west of this village. Make her an offering of fish, and you will then be ready for your performance.
1	line	Olaf the Bard	Make sure you give her a suitable offering however. If the offering is found to be unworthy, then you may find yourself unable to play your lyre with any skill at all!
1	line	Player	So what would be a worthy offering?
1	line	Olaf the Bard	A raw shark, manta ray, or sea turtle should be sufficient as an offering.
1	line	Player	Okay, what else do I need to do?
1	line	Olaf the Bard	When you have crafted your lyre and been blessed by Fossegrimen, then you will finally be ready to make your performance to the revellers at the longhall.
1	line	Olaf the Bard	Head past the bouncers and onto the stage, and then begin to play. If all goes well, you should find the music spring to your mind and sing your own epic on the spot.
1	line	Olaf the Bard	I will observe both you and the audience, and if you show enough talent, I will happily vote in your favour at the council of elders.
1	line	Olaf the Bard	Is that clear enough, outerlander? Would you like me to repeat anything?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Remind me about crafting a lyre
2	line	Player	Can you remind me about making a lyre again, please Olaf?
2	line	Olaf the Bard	There are three parts to making the lyre; First you need to cut some special wood from the special musical tree which can be found just east of Rellekka.
2	line	Olaf the Bard	When you have the wood, you will need to use a knife to craft it into a Lyre. When you have an unstrung lyre, you will need to string it before you can play it.
2	line	Olaf the Bard	I would not use anything other than the golden string of Lalli, a troll who lives in a cave just to the South-east.
2	line	Olaf the Bard	Is that clear enough, outerlander? Would you like me to repeat anything?
2	action	previous
1	option	Remind me about Fossegrimen
2	line	Player	Can you remind me about getting a blessing from Fossegrimen again?
2	line	Olaf the Bard	Certainly outerlander! Fossegrimen is a lake spirit who lives in the lake just to the South-west of here. She will bless you so that you may play your lyre,
2	line	Olaf the Bard	if you give her a worthy offering. She will only accept raw fish, so place a raw fish on her pedestal, and she will bless you. The better the offering, the longer
2	line	Olaf the Bard	the amount of time you will be blessed for. You will not be able to perform on stage without the blessing of the Fossegrimen.
2	line	Olaf the Bard	Is that clear enough, outerlander? Would you like me to repeat anything?
2	action	previous
1	option	Remind me about playing on stage
2	line	Player	Can you remind me about how to perform at the longhall again please?
2	line	Olaf the Bard	Not a problem outerlander. When you have your lyre and have been blessed, you will be able to pass the bouncer at the stage entrance of the longhall.
2	line	Olaf the Bard	He will not let you pass unless he believes you are ready to perform on stage. Simply go past him and onto the stage and use your lyre, and you will
2	line	Olaf the Bard	begin to play to entertain the revellers. If all has gone well, you will feel the music come to your mind, unbidden, as you sing an epic of your exploits.
2	line	Olaf the Bard	I will watch your performance from backstage, and also study how much the crowd likes you, and if I believe you have enough talent, then I will vote for you at the council.
2	line	Olaf the Bard	Is that clear enough, outerlander? Would you like me to repeat anything?
2	action	previous
1	option	I don't need a reminder
2	line	Player	No thanks, I think that's all pretty straight forward. I'll go and make my lyre now.
2	action	end
