0	section	Sigli the Huntsman
1	line	Sigli the Huntsman	What do you want outerlander?
1	line	Player	Are you a member of the council?
1	line	Sigli the Huntsman	The Fremennik council of elders? I am pleased to say that I am. My value as a huntsman is recognised by my position there.
1	line	Player	I was wondering if I could persuade you to vouch for me as a member of your clan?
1	line	Sigli the Huntsman	You? ... well... I am not totally against the idea outerlander. If you can demonstrate some hunting skills then perhaps I may offer my vote.
1	line	Player	How can I prove my hunting skills to you? I can go kill, like, a hundred chickens for you right now!
1	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Chickens? You think that would impress me?
1	line	Player	Cows then? I can kill cows until, er, the cows come home.
1	line	Sigli the Huntsman	No. The prey I have in mind for you to prove your worth to me is something far more dangerous. Far more difficult. Far more deadly.
1	line	Player	Not... Giant Rats?!?!
1	line	Sigli the Huntsman	I suspect you are mocking me outerlander. You will need to prove your skill as a hunter to me by tracking and defeating... The Draugen.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What's a Draugen?
2	line	Player	What's a Draugen? Some kind of cheap barbarian rip- off of a dragon?
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Hmmm. No, the words are slightly similar I suppose, but they are very different creatures.
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	The Draugen is an evil ghost from Fremennik mythology, that devours the souls of those brave warriors who meet their ends at sea.
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	It stalks the coastlines, invisible to all. It brings us bad fortunes, and curses our journeys across the seas. It is also unkillable by normal means.
2	line	Player	...Let me get this straight; You want me to hunt an unkillable, invincible, and invisible enemy? How am I supposed to do that?
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Well outerlander, should you accept my challenge I will show you a special hunter's trick that will help you. Do you accept the challenge?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Yes
3	line	Player	Well, I need every vote I can get in the council of elders, but this certainly sounds impossible to do...
3	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Not at all outerlander. The Draugen is indeed impossible to kill, but that is not the same as being impossible to fight against.
3	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Every time he takes a Fremennik life, he gains in power, so to keep it from becoming too powerful we hunters hunt it and steal its life force.
3	cond	If the player does not have inventory space:
4	line	Sigli the Huntsman	To defeat the Draugen you will need a special item; I have one to give you but it seems as though your inventory is too full to accept it.
4	action	end
3	cond	If the player has inventory space:
4	line	Sigli the Huntsman	We do this with a special talisman. Here, take it; it will let you track the Draugen while it's invisible, and when you defeat it will absorb its essence.
4	action	
4	line	Sigli the Huntsman	I want you to track the Draugen, defeat it, and store its essence in that talisman for me. If you can do this important task for my clan, I will vote for you.
4	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Take care of the talisman, and see me when you have completed this task.
4	action	end
2	option	No
3	line	Player	Forget it! This all sounds like way too much work for a stupid vote at a meeting! I'll find someone else instead.
3	action	end
