0	section	The Sailor's "Favor"
0	section	Talking to the Sailor
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find a rare flower from across the sea, do you?
2	line	Sailor	Ah! Even the outerlanders have heard of my mysterious flower! I found it in a country far far away from here!
2	line	Player	Can I buy it from you?
2	line	Sailor	I'm afraid not, outerlander. There is a woman in this village whose heart I seek to capture, and I think giving her this strange flower might be my best bet with her.
2	line	Player	Maybe you could let me have the flower and do something else to impress her?
2	line	Sailor	Hmm... that is not a totally stupid idea outerlander. I know she is a lover of music, and a romantic ballad might be just the thing with which to woo her.
2	line	Sailor	Unfortunately I don't have a musical bone in my entire body, so someone else will have to write it for me.
2	line	Player	So if I can find someone to write you a romantic ballad, you will give me your flower?
2	line	Sailor	That sounds like a fair deal to me, outerlander.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
0	section	Talking to Olaf the Bard
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find a love ballad, do you?
2	line	Olaf the Bard	Well, as official Fremennik bard, it falls within my remit to compose all music for the tribe. I am fully versed in all the various types of romantic music.
2	line	Player	Great! Can you write me one then?
2	line	Olaf the Bard	Well... normally I would be thrilled at the chance to show my skill as a poet in composing a seductively romantic ballad...
2	line	Player	let me guess; here comes the 'but'.
2	line	Olaf the Bard	...but unfortunately I cannot concentrate fully upon my work recently.
2	line	Player	Why is that then?
2	line	Olaf the Bard	It is these old worn out shoes of mine... As a bard I am expected to wander the lands, singing of the glorious battles of our warriors.
2	line	Olaf the Bard	If you can find me a pair of sturdy boots to replace these old worn out ones of mine, I will be happy to spend the time on composing you a romantic ballad.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
0	section	Talking to Yrsa
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find some custom sturdy boots, do you?
2	line	Yrsa	Well, I don't usually have many shoes in stock here in my little clothes shop... I will be able to make you up a pair if you are really desperate though?
2	line	Player	They're not for me... I need them for Olaf.
2	line	Yrsa	Oh, that foolish bard... Why didn't he just ask me to make him some? It is his stupid pride, I believe!
2	line	Yrsa	I will tell you what I will do outerlander; I know that you must have the ear of the chieftain for him to consider you as worthy of becoming a Fremennik by trial.
2	line	Yrsa	I will make you a pair of sturdy boots for Olaf if you will persuade him to reduce the sales tax placed upon all Fremennik shopkeepers. It does nothing but hurt my business now.
2	line	Player	Okay, I will see what I can do.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
0	section	Talking to Yrsa again
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find a guarantee of a reduction on sales taxes, do you?
2	line	Yrsa	Yes I do outerlander. Only the Chieftain may permit such a thing. Talk to him.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
0	section	Talking to Brundt
1	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Greetings again outerlander! How goes your attempts to gain votes with the council of elders?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find a guarantee of a reduction on sales taxes, do you?
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	A reduction on sales taxes? Why, I am the only one in the Fremennik who may authorise such a thing. What does an outerlander want with that?
2	line	Player	Actually, it's not for me. I need to get it as part of my trials.
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Hmmm. Interesting. Your trials seem to be very different to those I took as a young lad. Well, I am not adverse in principle to giving a slight tax break to our shops.
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	There will of course be a shortfall in the tribe's income, that will need to be made up for elsewhere, however.
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	How about this. For many years Sigli has been the only one in the tribe who knows the locations of the best hunting grounds where game is easiest to catch.
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	If you can persuade him to let the entire tribe know these hunting grounds, then we can increase productivity within the tribe, and any shortfall caused
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	by lowering sales taxes will be covered. I think this is a more than fair arrangement to make, don't you?
2	line	Player	Yeah, that sounds very fair.
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Speak to Sigli then, and you may have my promise to reduce our sales taxes. And best of luck with the rest of your trials.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
0	section	Finding Sigli's bowstring
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Greetings outerlander.
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find a map to unspoiled hunting grounds, do you?
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Well, of course I do. I wouldn't be much of a huntsman if I didn't know where to find my prey now, would I outerlander?
2	line	Player	No, I guess not. So can I have it?
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Directions to my hunting grounds could mean the end of my livelihood. The only way I would be prepared to give them up would be...
2	line	Player	What? Power? Money? Women? Wine?
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	...a new string for my hunting bow. Not just any bowstring; I need a custom bowstring, balanced for my bow precisely to keep my hunt competitive.
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	Only in this way would I allow the knowledge of my hunting grounds to be passed on to strangers.
2	line	Player	So where would I get that?
2	line	Sigli the Huntsman	I have no idea. But then again, I'm happy with my old bowstring and being the only person who knows where my hunting ground is.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	end
