1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
0	section	Convincing Thorvald to be a bodyguard
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find a brave and powerful warrior to act as a bodyguard?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Know you not who I am outerlander? There are none more brave or powerful than me amongst all the Fremennik!
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	However... The role of bodyguard is below me, as a noble warrior. You might as well ask me to babysit the children!
2	line	Player	Is there no way you would do this for me?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	There is but one way outerlander. Since I was steeled in battle, I have dreamt of earning my place at the Champions Table in the Long Hall.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	It is a tradition amongst us that the bravest and strongest are honoured with a table of champions to drink and feast all that they can in our Long Hall.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Unfortunately, there are only a fixed number of places available at the table, and these places were all filled many moons ago by others.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Although my worthiness is undeniable, the only way I may take my place is if one of those already there die, or give up their place to me voluntarily.
2	line	Player	So you want me to go kill one of them off for you? Make it look like an accident?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	WHAT? No, no, not at all! I am shocked you would suggest such a thing!
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	If you can persuade one of the Revellers to give up their Champions' Token to you so that I might take their place, you may have my contract as a bodyguard.
2	line	Player	Okay, I'll see what I can do.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
0	section	Talking to Thorvald again
