1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find a Champions' Token?
2	line	Thorvald	If you can persuade one of the Revellers to give up their Champions' Token to you so that I might take their place, you may have my contract as a bodyguard.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
0	section	Talking to Manni the Reveller
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find a token to allow a seat at the champions table, do you?
2	line	Manni the Reveller	As a matter of fact, I do. I have one right here. I earnt my place here at the longhall for surviving over 5000 battles and raiding parties.
2	line	Manni the Reveller	Due to my contribution to the tribe, I am now permitted to spend my days here in the longhall listening to the epic tales of the bard, and drinking beer.
2	line	Player	Cool. That sounds pretty sweet! So I guess you don't want to give it away?
2	line	Manni the Reveller	I think it sounds better than it actually is outerlander. I miss my glory days of combat on the battlefield. And to tell you the truth, the beer here isn't great, and the bards' music is lousy.
2	line	Manni the Reveller	I would happily give up my token if it were not for the one thing that keeps me here. Our barkeep is one of the best in the world, and has worked in taverns across the land.
2	line	Manni the Reveller	When she was younger, she experimented a lot with her drinks, and invented a cocktail so alcoholic and tasty that it has become something of a legend to all who enjoy a drink.
2	line	Manni the Reveller	Unfortunately, she decided that cocktails were not a suitable drink for Fremennik warriors, and vowed to never again make it.
2	line	Manni the Reveller	I have been here every day since she returned, hoping that someday she might change her mind and I might try this legendary cocktail for myself. Alas, it has never come to pass...
2	line	Manni the Reveller	If you can persuade her to make me her legendary cocktail, I will be happy to never let another drop of alcohol pass my lips, and will give you my champions token.
2	line	Player	That's all?
2	line	Manni the Reveller	That's all.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
0	section	Talking to Manni again
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find the longhall barkeeps' legendary cocktail, do you?
2	line	Manni the Reveller	Uh... yes, the longhall barkeep has it. So could you get me my drink now please?
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
0	section	Talking to Thora
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	line	Player	I don't suppose you have any idea where I could find the longhall barkeeps' legendary cocktail, do you?
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	How did you hear about that?!?!?
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	I didn't think anybody knew about that... Well, it is true that in my younger years as a barkeep, I wandered the lands trying various alcoholic delicacies.
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	Did you ever realise just how many different types of alcohol there are here in Gielinor? Lots!
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	Well, anyway, I used a fusion of various drinks from all around the world to create the greatest cocktail ever made!
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	Of course, when my wanderlust was gone, and I returned back to Rellekka to serve as barkeep here, I gave all that up.
2	line	Player	But you still remember how to make it, right?
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	Of course.
2	line	Player	And you have all the ingredients here? I don't need to go chasing round the world for obscure ingredients to make it?
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	No, I have them all here. Why?
2	line	Player	Can you make me your legendary cocktail then?
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	I would rather not; it is a reminder of a life I left behind when I came back.
2	line	Player	Any way I could change your mind?
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	You need this to become a Fremennik, right? Well, you seem okay for an outerlander, it would be a shame to see you fail. You know Askeladden?
2	line	Player	That kid outside? Sure.
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	He is nothing but a pest. He keeps sneaking in and stealing beer. I shudder to think what he will be like when he has passed his trial of manhood,
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	and is allowed in here legitimately. If you can get him to sign a contract promising that he will NEVER EVER EVER darken my doorway here again, you get the drink.
2	line	Player	Any idea how I can get him to do that?
2	line	Thora the Barkeep	Knowing that little horror, he'll probably be willing to in exchange for some cash. You should go ask him yourself though.
2	action	end
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
