0	section	Thorvald the Warrior
1	line	Player	Hello!
1	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Hello yourself, outerlander. What brings you to dare speak to a mighty Fremennik warrior such as myself?
1	line	Player	Erm... are you a member of the council?
1	line	Thorvald the Warrior	The Fremennik council of elders? Why, of course I am. I am recognised as one the clans mightiest warriors. What is it to you outerlander?
1	line	Player	Well... I was wondering if you could vote for me to become a Fremennik.
1	line	Thorvald the Warrior	An outerlander wishes to become a Fremennik!?!? Ha! That is priceless!
1	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Well, let us say that I am not totally against this concept. As a warrior, I appreciate the value of brave and powerful warriors to our clan,
1	line	Thorvald the Warrior	and even though you may be an outerlander, I will not hold this against you if you can prove yourself to be fierce of heart in a combat situation to me.
1	line	Player	So how can I prove that? You want to fight me? Come on then, bring it on! Right here, right now, buddy!
1	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Hahahahaha! You certainly show some spirit for an outerlander!
1	line	Thorvald the Warrior	But spirit does not always make a good warrior. It takes both skill and spirit to be so. I have a test that I give all Fremenniks on their path to be a member of the clan.
1	line	Thorvald the Warrior	My test will challenge both your combat prowess and your bravery equally. Should you pass it you will earn my vote at the council, and more importantly my respect for you as a warrior.
1	line	Thorvald the Warrior	So what say you, outerlander? Are you prepared for the battle?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Yes
2	line	Player	Am I prepared? I'll show you what combat's all about, you big sissy barbarian type guy!
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Hahahahaha! I'm beginning to like you already, outerlander!
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Then allow me to present you with my challenge; This ladder here will take you to a place of combat. I have placed a special warrior down there to challenge you.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Battle him to the death, and you will pass my challenge. If at any point you wish to leave combat, simply climb back up the ladder, to leave that place.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	If you leave you will of course fail the test. You may retry my test in the future if you fail, but you must stay down there until the death if you wish for my vote at the council.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	You must defeat him three times to prove that you are worthy. The fourth time that you fight him will be to the death, so do not show cowardice.
2	line	Player	Is that all? It will be easy!
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	No, there is one more important rule;
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	You may not enter the battleground with any armour or weaponry of any kind.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	If you need to place your equipment into your bank account, I recommend that you speak to the seer, who knows a spell that will do that for you.
2	action	end
1	option	No
2	line	Player	No thanks, I'm pretty sure that I can find someone else to vote for me.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Hmm, not so brave after all, outerlander? Perhaps it is for the best. I doubt you have what it takes to pass my challenge.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Thorvald again
1	select	Select an option
1	option	What do I have to do again?
2	line	Player	So what do I have to do to earn your vote at the council again?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	I will not offer my vote to anybody whose bravery in combat I do not trust completely. You must go down that ladder and fight your foe to the death.
2	action	end
1	option	Who is my opponent?
2	line	Player	So, who is my opponent?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Ah, a wise question before entering combat. His name is Koschei the deathless. He is something of a mystery, even to us.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	On one of our regular raiding parties, our longship discovered a man in the frozen waters far north-east of here. We took him aboard our ship, thinking he must be dead.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	To our amazement he was perfectly healthy, even though he must have been in those deadly icy waters for many weeks.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	He has no memory of who he is, or how he came to be there, except for his own name: Koschei. We named him 'The Deathless' because he is seemingly unkillable!
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Any combat technique used against him, he learns instantly! He also apparently can heal himself from any wound at will! When he attacks, his weapon moves like a whirlwind!
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	He can hide his combat level from his opponents at will as well! He is truly a horribly fierce opponent to face! I am only glad that he has chosen to stay here with us!
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	The daylight makes him feel weak, so we have built him his own battleground beneath this building, where he can train his fiercesome skills without being disturbed.
2	line	Player	But he can't REALLY be unkillable... ...can he?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Some say he cannot die, for he has hidden his heart outside of his body to be kept forever safe in a duck egg.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Others say he has been cursed by the gods to wander this land forever, never knowing any peace in his life, but only combat.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Some claim that the sword he carries is the source of all his power, and if he should lose it, then exactly one minute later, he will turn back into his true form;
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	A weakened, lame, old man.
2	line	Player	And what do you believe?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	I believe you shouldn't look a gift horse in the mouth. He is a fearfully powerful warrior, but more importantly; He is on OUR side, not against us.
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	He is content testing the battle skills of anyone taking their Fremennik trials of manhood, and I am content knowing that should an enemy ever invade our town,
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	while our warriors are out on a raiding party, Koschei will be able to hold off ANY invader long enough for us to make our return.
1	option	Can't I do something else?
2	line	Player	I don't really like fighting that much... Isn't there something else I can do to earn your vote at the council of elders?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Yes of course outerlander! If you bring me five raw sardines then I will vote for you instead!
2	line	Player	REALLY?!?!?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	HAHAHAHAHAHA! No, of course not! You are stupid, even by outerlander standards!
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	If you want my vote, you must pass my trial. It is as simple as that.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player attempts to use a raw sardine on Thorvald:
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	I was only joking about the raw sardines outerlander.
2	line	Player	Oh. Really? Oh. So I have to pass your combat trial?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Yes.
2	action	end
0	section	Peer the Seer
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Ask about the Merchant's trial
2	action	above
1	option	Ask about becoming a Fremennik
2	action	above
1	option	Ask about depositing your equipment
2	line	Player	Hello there! Thorvald tells me you can deposit my equipment directly into my bank account for me...?
2	line	Peer the Seer	That is correct outerlander, but you will need to go and retrieve your equipment from your bank account yourself, manually.
2	line	Peer the Seer	Alas, my spell is not very accurate, so it will deposit everything you have upon you into your bank, not just your armour and weapons.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Bank your equipment
3	line	Player	Yes, please deposit my equipment.
3	cond	If the player's bank is full or if the player has unbankable items (e.g. a Lamp or experience tome):
4	line	Peer the Seer	I am sorry outerlander, the spell is not working.
4	action	end
3	cond	If the player's bank is not full:
4	action	Peer the seer banks all of the player's contents from their inventory and worn equipment.
4	line	Peer the Seer	The task is done. I wish you luck with your test, outerlander.
4	action	end
2	option	Don't bank your equipment
3	line	Player	No thanks, I'll just go to the bank and sort my inventory out myself.
3	action	end
