2	action	end
0	section	Koschei's random dialogue
1	option	Dialogue 1
2	line	Koschei the deathless	Prepare to die, {player}!
1	option	Dialogue 2
2	line	Koschei the deathless	I will crush your dead bones!
1	option	Dialogue 3
2	line	Koschei the deathless	Outerlander... you have made a mistake coming down here!
1	option	Dialogue 4
2	line	Koschei the deathless	What kind of a person calls [him/her]self {player}?
1	option	Dialogue 5
2	line	Koschei the deathless	You have no idea of my true power, outerlander!
1	option	Dialogue 6
2	line	Koschei the deathless	Today is the day you die, outerlander!
1	option	Dialogue 7
2	line	Koschei the deathless	{player}! Meet your doom!
1	option	Dialogue 8
2	line	Koschei the deathless	Prepare to face my power, outerlander!
0	section	After defeating Koschei
0	section	Talking to Thorvald
1	cond	If the player does not manage to defeat Koschei's fourth phase:
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Hahaha! Well fought outerlander! Now come down from there, you have passed my trial with flying colours!
2	line	Player	But... I don't understand... I did not manage to beat Koschei...
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	I would be honoured to represent you to the council as worthy of being a Fremennik after watching that superb battle!
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player manages to defeat Koschei:
2	line	Player	So can I count on your vote at the council of elders now Thorvald?
2	line	Thorvald the Warrior	Absolutely! I watched the entire battle, and was extremely impressed with your bravery in combat!
2	action	end
0	section	Attempting to climb down the stairs again
1	line	Player	I'd really rather not go back down there again, now that I have Thorvald's vote at the council of elders.
1	action	end
0	section	Peer the Seer's Trial
1	line	Peer the Seer	Hello outerlander. What do you want?
1	line	Player	Hello. I'm looking for members of the council of elders to vote for me to become a Fremennik.
1	line	Peer the Seer	Are you now? Well that is interesting. Usually outerlanders do not concern themselves with our ways like that.
1	line	Peer the Seer	I am one of the members of the council of elders, and should you be able to prove to me that you have something to offer my clan
1	line	Peer the Seer	I will vote in your favour at the next meeting.
1	line	Player	How can I prove that to you?
1	line	Peer the Seer	Well, I have but a simple test. This building behind me is my house. Inside I have constructed a puzzle.
1	line	Peer the Seer	As a Seer to the clan, I value intelligence very highly, so you may think of it as an intelligence test of sorts.
1	line	Player	An intelligence test? I thought barbarians were stupid!
1	line	Peer the Seer	That is the opinion that outerlanders usually hold of my people, it is true. But that is because people often confuse knowledge with wisdom.
1	line	Peer the Seer	My puzzle tests not what you know, but what you can work out. All members of our clan have been tested when they took their trials.
1	line	Player	So what exactly does this puzzle consist of, then?
1	line	Peer the Seer	Well, firstly you must enter my house with no items, weapons or armour. Then it is a simple matter of entering through one door and leaving by the other.
1	line	Player	I can't take anything in there with me?
1	line	Peer the Seer	That is correct outerlander. Everything you need to complete the puzzle you will find inside the building. Nothing more.
1	line	Peer the Seer	So what say you outerlander? You think you have the wit to earn yourself my vote?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Yes
2	line	Player	Yes, I accept your challenge. I have one small question, however...
2	line	Peer the Seer	Yes, outerlander?
2	line	Player	Well... you say I can bring nothing with me when I enter your house...
2	line	Peer the Seer	Yes, outerlander?
2	line	Player	Well.....
2	line	Peer the Seer	Yes, outerlander?
2	line	Player	Where is the nearest bank?
2	line	Peer the Seer	Ah, I see your problem outerlander. The nearest bank to here is the place known to outerlanders as the Seers Village. It is some way South.
2	line	Peer the Seer	I do however have an alternative, should you wish to take it.
2	line	Player	And what is that?
2	line	Peer the Seer	I can store all the weapons, armour and items that you have upon you directly into your bank account.
2	line	Peer the Seer	This will tax what little magic I possess however, so you will have to manually travel to the bank to withdraw them again.
2	line	Peer the Seer	What say you outerlander? you wish me to do this for you?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Yes
3	line	Player	Yes, thank you!
3	action	The player's items in their inventory and worn items are deposited into their bank.
3	line	Peer the Seer	The task is done. I wish you luck with your test, outerlander.
3	action	end
2	option	No
3	line	Player	No thanks. Nobody touches my stuff but me!
3	line	Peer the Seer	As you wish, outerlander.
3	line	Peer the Seer	You may attempt my little task when you have deposited your equipment in the bank.
2	action	end
1	option	No
2	line	Player	No, thinking about stuff isn't really my 'thing'. I'd rather go kill something. I'll find someone else to vote for me.
2	line	Peer the Seer	As you wish, outerlander.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Peer the Seer again
1	cond	If the player has items in their inventory and/or wearing any armour:
2	line	Player	So I can bring nothing with me when I enter your house?
2	line	Peer the Seer	That is correct outerlander, but as I say, I can use my small skill in magic to send your items directly into your bank account from here.
2	line	Peer the Seer	You will need to manually go to the bank to withdraw them again however. Would you like me to perform this small spell upon you, outerlander?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Yes
3	action	above
2	option	No
3	action	above
1	cond	If the player does not have any items in their inventory or in their worn slots:
2	line	Player	So I just have to enter by one door of your house, and leave by the other?
2	line	Peer the Seer	That is correct outerlander. Be warned it is not as easy as it may at first sound...
2	action	end
0	section	The Riddle
1	cond	If the player enters Peer the Seer's house on the east side:
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player enters Peer the Seer's house on the west side:
2	box	There is a combination lock on this door. Above the lock you can see that there is a metal plaque with a riddle on it.
2	select	What would you like to do?
2	option	Read the riddle
3	option	Riddle 1
4	box	My first is in the well, but not at sea. My second in 'I', but not in 'me'. My third is in flies, but insects not found. My last is in earth, but not in the ground.
4	box	My whole when stolen from you, causes you death. What am I?
3	option	Riddle 2
4	box	My first is in water, and also in tea. My second in fish, but not in the sea. My third in mountains, but not underground. My last is in strike, but not in pound.
4	box	My whole crushes mountains, drains rivers, and destroys civilisations. All that live fear my passing. What am I?
3	option	Riddle 3
4	box	My first is in mage, but not in wizard. My second in goblin, and also in lizard. My third in night, but not in the day. My last is in fields, but not in the hay.
4	box	My whole is the most powerful tool you will possess. What am I?
3	option	Riddle 4
4	box	My first is in tar, but not in a swamp. My second in fire, but not in a camp. My third is in eagle, but never in air. My last is in hate, but also in care.
4	box	My whole wears rings the older I get. What am I?
3	option	Riddle 5
4	box	My first is in fish, but not in the sea. My second in birds, but not in the sea. My third is in mountains, but not underground. My last is everything, but not at all.
4	box	My whole cannot die as long as it has food. What am I?
3	option	Riddle 6
4	box	My first is in wizard, but not in a mage. My second in jail, but not in a cage. My third is in anger, but not in a rage. My last in a drawing, but not on a page.
4	box	My whole helps to make bread, let birds fly and boats sail. What am I?
3	cond	If the player fails to solve the puzzle:
4	action	end
3	cond	If the player solves the riddle:
4	action	end
2	option	Solve the riddle
3	cond	If the player enters the wrong code:
4	action	above
3	cond	If the player enters the correct code:
4	action	above
2	option	Forget it
3	action	end
1	cond	If the player enters the door and attempts to leave:
2	box	If you leave by this door you will fail this trial. Press continue to go through the door anyway.
2	cond	If the player presses continue:
3	action	All of the items gathered in the room are gone.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player clicks anywhere else in the house:
3	action	The puzzle resumes.
3	action	end
