1	action	end
0	section	Swensen's Trial
0	section	Attempting to climb down the ladder or trapdoor before accepting the challenge
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	Have you no manners outerlander? This is my home, you will show me the due respect!
1	line	Player	Erm.... sorry I guess.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Swensen
1	line	Player	Hello!
1	line	Player	I am trying to become a member of the Fremennik clan! The Chieftain told me that I may be able to gain your vote at the council of elders?
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	You wish to stop being an outerlander? I can understand that! I have no reason why I would prevent you becoming a Fremennik...
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	...but you must first pass a little test for me to prove you are worthy.
1	line	Player	What kind of test?
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	Well, I serve our clan as a navigator. The seas can be a fearful place when you know not where you are heading.
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	Should something happen to me, all members of our tribe have some basic sense of direction so that they may always return safely home.
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	If you are able to demonstrate to me that you too have a good sense of direction then I will recommend you to the rest of the council of elders immediately.
1	line	Player	Well, how would I go about showing that?
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	Ah, a simple task! Below this building I have constructed a maze; should you be able to walk from one side to the other that will be proof to me.
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	You wish to try my challenge?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Yes
2	line	Player	A maze? Is that all? Sure, it sounds simple enough.
2	line	Swensen the Navigator	I will warn you outerlander, this maze was designed by myself, and is of the most fiendish complexity!
2	line	Player	Oh really? Watch and learn...
2	action	end
1	option	No
2	line	Player	No thanks. I think I can get someone else to vouch for me to the council of elders, without going through a stupid maze like some lab rat.
2	line	Swensen the Navigator	Well, I am sorry you feel that way outerlander. I cannot vouch for you until you prove to me you have some skill that will benefit our clan somehow.
2	line	Swensen the Navigator	What exactly is a 'lab rat' anyway?
2	line	Player	Ah, forget it.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Swensen again
1	line	Player	Hello!
1	line	Player	Man, your maze is pretty tough!
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	Hahahaha it is the most complex route I have ever devised! I am truly a genius at navigation! The world will remember my name!
1	line	Player	Can't I do something else for your vote at the council of elders?
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	No, you cannot. It is my maze, or nothing.
1	action	end
0	section	Entering the maze
1	cond	If the player attempts to enter through any of the trapdoors:
2	box	You try to open the trapdoor but it won't budge! It looks like the trapdoor can only be opened from the other side.
2	action	end
1	cond	If the player climbs down the ladder:
2	action	continue
0	section	Whilst inside the maze
1	cond	If the player leaves through the escape rope:
2	line	Swensen the Navigator	Decided you could not solve my labyrinth after all, did you outerlander? Too tricky for you?
2	line	Player	Yeah, it is really confusing down there...
2	line	Swensen the Navigator	Hahaha! Don't worry outerlander, you are not the first to fail its puzzle!
1	action	end
1	cond	If the player climbs up the stairs in the north-western portal room:
2	line	Swensen the Navigator	Outerlander! You have finished my maze! I am genuinely impressed!
2	line	Player	So does that mean I can rely on your vote at the council of elders to allow me into your village?
2	line	Swensen the Navigator	Of course outerlander! I am nothing if not a man of my word!
2	line	Player	Thanks!
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Swensen again
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	Greetings again outerlander! I must say, I am still impressed with the way you moved through my maze!
1	line	Player	Thanks. So I can rely on your vote in my favour at the council of elders?
1	line	Swensen the Navigator	Absolutely! You will be an asset to the clan!
1	action	end
1	cond	If the player attempts to climb down into the maze again:
2	line	Player	No way am I doing that maze again!
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Brundt
1	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Greetings again outerlander! How goes your attempts to gain votes with the council of elders?
1	cond	If the player has not gotten only one vote:
2	line	Player	I only have 1 vote so far.
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Hmmm... well that is certainly a good start I would say. Keep up the good work!
2	action	continue
1	cond	If the player has gotten 2-6 votes:
2	line	Player	I only have [2-6] votes so far.
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Hmmm... you are doing very well so far, outerlander. Keep up the good work!
2	action	continue
1	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Remember: You need to get at least seven council votes to be accepted as a member of the Fremennik.
1	line	Brundt the Chieftain	If you need any help with your trials, I suggest you speak to Askeladden. He is currently doing his own trials of manhood to become a true Fremennik.
1	action	end
1	cond	If the player has gotten all 7 votes:
2	line	Player	I have seven members of the council prepared to vote in my favour now!
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	I know outerlander, for I have been closely monitoring your progress so far!
2	line	Brundt the Chieftain	Then let us put the formality aside, and let me personally welcome you into the Fremennik! May you bring us honour!
0	section	Post-quest dialogue
1	line	Brundt the Chieftain	From this day onward, you are outerlander no more! In honour of your acceptance into the Fremennik You gain a new name to be known as. You will now be called [Fremennik name].
1	action	end
